        "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14209261/assets/5270ae4ee5e310d1a28569a26ca5c9adef4c1e3c8af0db159385b0104d160f43.png)\n\nConsider the functions $f(x),$ $g(x),$ and $h(x)$ defined below. A part of the graph of $y=h(x)$ on the interval $x\\in [-3,2]$ is depicted above.\n\n$$\nf(x)=3\\sqrt{x}+2,\\,g(x)=2x-6,\\,h(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3-(x+1)^{2}, & \\,x<0 \\\\ 2x+1, & \\,x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
